    "question": {
      ":question/id": "4cf49f8b-f9cc-534f-91ca-81fc4b37f77d",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate the integral $\\int x{4}^{3{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "6e4301a9-c5ce-5b58-bd47-3030898abac1",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "0f4fce80-c739-5559-8aba-b057a280fa5d",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{4^{3 x^{2}}}{\\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}+C"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "c8e2530f-87ac-51f6-8fb4-314474a306d7",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{4^{3 x^{2}}}{6 \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}+C"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "12e57e0b-4804-5945-b328-416bad2c6b3a",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{6 \\cdot 4^{3 x^{2}}}{\\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}+C"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "555e25d4-54c4-53af-8341-10c0b66c1a4e",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{4^{3 x^{2}}}{6}+C"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "7e179f8b-1a25-5bae-8eef-7a5ba1039724",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{4^{3 x^{2}} \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}{6}+C"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "c8e2530f-87ac-51f6-8fb4-314474a306d7"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's introduce the new variable $u=3{x}^{2}.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{4}^{3{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {4}^{3{x}^{2}}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {4}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\int {4}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\frac{{4}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{4}^{3{x}^{2}}}{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
