      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's introduce the new variable $u=4 - 3 x^{4}.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=- 12 x^{3}\\,⟹\\,\\left(- \\frac{1}{12}\\right)\\text{d}u=x^{3}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x^{3}\\,{4}^{4 - 3 x^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {4}^{4 - 3 x^{4}}\\cdot x^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\int {4}^{u}\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{1}{12}\\right)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\left(- \\frac{1}{12}\\right)\\int {4}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\left(- \\frac{1}{12}\\right)\\cdot\\frac{{4}^{u}}{\\ln 4}+C \\\\ & =- \\frac{4^{4 - 3 x^{4}}}{12 \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
